{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085950-antagonists-for-cofd-2e","id":1085950,"title":"Antagonists for CofD 2E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-30T17:03:04-07:00","id":1085950,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Antagonists for CofD 2E","content":"I am looking for material on Antagonists for CoD 2E, i.e. material on how to create them. There is a little bit in the core books I have, but that feels like partial system write ups. Has anyone done some work fleshing it out? Am I just missing something?<br /> <br /> Any info would be appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T17:29:25-07:00","id":1085959,"title":"","content":"Which part in core did you mean? Character Creation, Horror rules, Ephemeral Entities? I can't remember is they have sample NPCs, but I know a list is around somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T17:45:28-07:00","id":1085968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085950-antagonists-for-cofd-2e#post1085950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I just missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends.<br /> <br /> If you're talking about normal human antagonists, it has examples and says you should alter the numbers of things if they don't match what you want precisely etc. And they are only partial statblocks, because there is no reason to have full-statblocks for NPCs as if they were PC's because 99% of the time the stuff that is missing either wont come up or will be very specific to the individual so makes no sense to be in a generic statblock. There are no precise rules for making these sort of NPCs since they basically use the same rules as any other human character, except you can just fudge some numbers for speed and because sometimes it'll make more sense for the story. <br /> <br /> Ephemeral Creatures and Horrors have detailed rules for creating them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T17:45:52-07:00","id":1085970,"title":"","content":"Character creation and the material on ephemeral entities is fine (although I do wish the Mage book had more Numina).<br /> <br /> There are a couple sample NPCs, but no rules for how they created them. Although, while I was sitting here thinking about it, they may have used the full rules for character creation and used some kind of &quot;short hand&quot; for the sample characters. If that is the case, I accidentally tricked myself into thinking there was something more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T18:15:43-07:00","id":1085983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1085950-antagonists-for-cofd-2e?p=1085968#post1085968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends.<br /> <br /> If you're talking about normal human antagonists, it has examples and says you should alter the numbers of things if they don't match what you want precisely etc. And they are only partial statblocks, because there is no reason to have full-statblocks for NPCs as if they were PC's because 99% of the time the stuff that is missing either wont come up or will be very specific to the individual so makes no sense to be in a generic statblock. There are no precise rules for making these sort of NPCs since they basically use the same rules as any other human character, except you can just fudge some numbers for speed and because sometimes it'll make more sense for the story.<br /> <br /> Ephemeral Creatures and Horrors have detailed rules for creating them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}